    <bpmn:process id="W_W1938" name="W1938. VMI Stock Level Monitoring &amp; Exception Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily VMI stock level monitoring
Frequency: Daily monitoring; weekly review
Volume: ~300 VMI SKUs × ~205 locations
Owner: VP Supply Chain
Participants: VP Supply Chain, Buyer, Vendor
Source: workflow W1938 — VMI Stock Level Monitoring &amp; Exception Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1938_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1938_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1938_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1938_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1938_Lane2" name="VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1938_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1938_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1938_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1938_Start4" name="Daily VMI stock level monitoring">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1938_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1938_Task5" name="System monitors VMI stock levels daily: (a) flag SKUs below minimum level…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System monitors VMI stock levels daily: (a) flag SKUs below minimum level (stockout risk), (b) flag SKUs above maximum level (overstock risk), (c) flag SKUs at zero stock (immediate action needed), (d) flag SKUs with consistent above-max pattern (parameter adjustment needed)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1938_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1938_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1938_Task6" name="VP Supply Chain reviews exceptions: (a) below-min: did vendor replenish? If…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VP Supply Chain reviews exceptions: (a) below-min: did vendor replenish? If not, escalate to vendor with SLA breach notice, (b) above-max: did vendor over-ship? Request return or adjust future orders, (c) zero stock: emergency replenishment — expedite from vendor or transfer from another location per W22
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30–60 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1938_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1938_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1938_Task7" name="Weekly: VP Supply Chain conducts VMI exception review with Category Manager…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Weekly: VP Supply Chain conducts VMI exception review with Category Manager: (a) top 10 stockout SKUs by lost sales estimate, (b) top 10 overstock SKUs by excess value, (c) vendor response time to replenishment triggers, (d) adjust VMI parameters if systemic issues identified
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1938_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1938_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1938_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1938_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1938_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-377 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor-Managed Inventory (VMI) Operations (PA-45.2).) | - operational: VP Supply Chain review and approval gate
Owner: VP Supply Chain</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
