    <bpmn:process id="W_W1939" name="W1939. VMI New Product Introduction &amp; Phase-Out" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New product launch; product phase-out decision
Frequency: ~20–30 VMI SKU changes/year
Volume: ~300 VMI SKUs managed
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, VP Supply Chain, Vendor
Source: workflow W1939 — VMI New Product Introduction &amp; Phase-Out</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1939_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1939_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1939_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1939_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1939_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1939_End6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1939_Start3" name="New product launch; product phase-out decision">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1939_Flow9</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1939_Task4" name="New VMI product introduction: (a) Category Manager adds new SKU to VMI…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: New VMI product introduction: (a) Category Manager adds new SKU to VMI agreement, (b) VP Supply Chain configures VMI parameters (min/max/ROP/ROQ) based on similar product demand history, (c) initial stock: vendor ships initial fill within 2 weeks of SKU activation, (d) monitor closely for first 4 weeks: compare actual demand to parameter assumptions
Responsible (R): Category Manager / VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1939_Flow9</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1939_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1939_Task5" name="VMI product phase-out: (a) Category Manager flags SKU for phase-out in VMI…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VMI product phase-out: (a) Category Manager flags SKU for phase-out in VMI agreement, (b) vendor stops replenishment, (c) remaining VMI stock sold through normally (or returned to vendor per agreement), (d) once stock reaches zero: remove from VMI parameters, (e) if significant remaining stock: negotiate vendor buyback or markdown support
Responsible (R): Category Manager / VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 weeks/phase-out</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1939_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1939_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1939_End6" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1939_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
